WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.768
Open WebUI can support document and knowledge workflows where uploaded material is used as context for model responses.

00:00:07.768 --> 00:00:16.712
At a high level, retrieval-augmented generation involves indexing or retrieving relevant content and placing it into the model's context.

00:00:16.712 --> 00:00:20.172
Embeddings help represent text for similarity search.

00:00:20.172 --> 00:00:26.700
This can make private documents more usable, but it also creates new data handling responsibilities.

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:30.356
Document sensitivity should be considered before upload.

00:00:30.356 --> 00:00:39.887
Files may contain personal information, client data, business plans, credentials, internal procedures, regulated content, or proprietary research.

00:00:39.887 --> 00:00:45.893
Once uploaded, they may be stored, indexed, backed up, searched, or reused in conversations.

00:00:45.893 --> 00:00:51.833
Treat document features as part of a data management system, not just a convenience button.

00:00:51.833 --> 00:00:55.620
Source organization improves retrieval quality and review.

00:00:55.620 --> 00:01:01.756
Knowledge collections should have clear names, purpose, ownership, and freshness expectations.

00:01:01.756 --> 00:01:04.694
Stale documents can produce outdated answers.

00:01:04.694 --> 00:01:09.133
Inaccurate retrieval can surface irrelevant or conflicting material.

00:01:09.133 --> 00:01:15.204
Retrieved content should be treated as evidence for the model to use, not unquestioned truth.

00:01:15.204 --> 00:01:17.097
Retention and cleanup matter.

00:01:17.097 --> 00:01:26.367
Decide how long uploaded documents should remain, who can access them, how they are removed, and whether backups preserve them after deletion.

00:01:26.367 --> 00:01:35.115
For important workflows, users should be able to trace an answer back to source material and understand whether the source is current.

00:01:35.115 --> 00:01:38.575
Retrieval is most valuable when it remains auditable.
